    "title": "Woodstock Midday Optimist Club donates $500 and food to CCHVP - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Staff reports ,\n14 hours ago The Woodstock Midday Optimist Club presented a $500 check and food donations to the Cherokee County Homeless Veterans Program. From left to right: CCHVP Executive Director Jim Lindenmayer, Alessandra Elliott, Doug Breckenridge and William Hicks. By Woodstock Midday Optimist Club The Woodstock Midday Optimist Club recently presented a $500 check and food donations to the Cherokee County Homeless Veterans Program.\nThe club reported that its food donations were worth about $500.\nCCHVP has opened a food pantry for active duty military personnel living in Cherokee County who have lost Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program benefits, or food stamps. The pantry is open 10 a.m. to 2 p.m. Monday, Wednesday and Friday at Thomas M. Brady American Legion Post 45, 160 McClure St. in Canton.",
